          "id" : "CVE-2025-69993",
          "shortDescription" : {
            "text" : "medium severity - CVE-2025-69993 Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:npm/leaflet@1.9.4"
          },
          "fullDescription" : {
            "text" : "Leaflet versions up to and including 1.9.4 are vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) via the bindPopup() method. This method renders user-supplied input as raw HTML without sanitization, allowing attackers to inject arbitrary JavaScript code through event handler attributes (e.g., <img src=x onerror=\"alert('XSS')\">). When a victim views an affected map popup, the malicious script executes in the context of the victim's browser session."
          },
